    ["BrenoBertucci/Terrarium"] = {
      checkedAt = 1786730316,
      latest = "1.19.0",
      releases = {
        [1] = {
          body = "# Terrarium\13\
\13\
A little world under glass: weather, day/night, and a full 3D diorama overworld for Gen1Recomp.\13\
\13\
## Fork notice\13\
\13\
**Terrarium is a fork of [Dramatic Shape Voxel Mod](https://github.com/DramaticShape/DramaticShapeVoxelMod) by [DramaticShape](https://github.com/DramaticShape).** The diorama, depth-buffered occlusion, shadow map, tilt-shift, and over-the-shoulder battles are his work. Look at the original first if you are choosing between them.\13\
\13\
This fork is **independent**: different mod id (`TERRARIUM`), different install folder, different pipeline registry keys (`terrarium_voxel` / `terrarium_tiltshift`), and letter hotkeys so it can sit **beside** upstream `DRAMATIC_SHAPE` without overwriting it or fighting its digit hotkeys.\13\
\13\
## Install\13\
\13\
1. Import the release zip through FIND MODS / Import, or drop the folder into `mods/TERRARIUM`.\13\
2. Enable **Terrarium** in the mod manager.\13\
3. Optional: keep **Dramatic Shape Voxel Mod** installed too -- they do not share folder or id.\13\
\13\
## Hotkeys (this fork)\13\
\13\
| Key | Action |\13\
|-----|--------|\13\
| `v` | VOXEL camera ladder |\13\
| `g` | V-GRID wireframe |\13\
| `t` | T-SHIFT miniature blur |\13\
| `c` | V-CURVE horizon |\13\
| `b` | 3D-BTL overworld battles |\13\
| `n` | WILD roam mode |\13\
| `p` | Minimap |\13\
| `h` | V-HAZE aerial perspective |\13\
| `k` | HORIZON far silhouettes |\13\
\13\
Upstream Dramatic Shape still uses `3` / `5` / `6` / `7` / `8` / `9`.\13\
\13\
## Features (high level)\13\
\13\
- 3D extruded overworld with cast shadows and tilt-shift\13\
- Day/night cycle, weather, puddles and snow on the ground\13\
- Wild Pokemon visible in the grass; ecology / shelter / city life systems\13\
- Tuned defaults for lower-end / mobile hardware\13\
\13\
## New in 1.19.0-mobile\13\
\13\
The sky, and how far away everything is.\13\
\13\
- **You can see the rain coming.** A curtain of it stands on the horizon as\13\
  vertical shafts, and it fills in while the drops near you are still nothing\13\
  -- so the weather arrives as something you watch approach for the better\13\
  part of a minute instead of something that switches on.\13\
- **Clouds travel over Kanto, not over your monitor.** The deck reads the\13\
  camera now, and it shifts *less* than everything else on screen, which is\13\
  what makes it read as far away. It also changes shape while it drifts,\13\
  instead of being one rigid pattern towed past.\13\
- **God rays after a shower**, thrown where the deck is breaking up -- light\13\
  through the gaps, not a glow pasted over the sun. In hard steps with the\13\
  same dither as the rest of the sky, so it stays painted rather than bloomed.\13\
- **A storm sky.** Heavy rain now bruises the sky violet instead of only\13\
  greying it -- and only the rain heavy enough to throw lightning does, so a\13\
  purple sky is a promise. A drizzle looks exactly as it always did.\13\
- **Stars go out one at a time** as cloud comes over, scattered, faint ones\13\
  first, rather than the whole field dimming together.\13\
- **V-HAZE** (`h`): the far ground goes paler and bluer with distance. Equal\13\
  contrast reads as equal distance, and that one cue is most of why a map used\13\
  to feel the size of one screen.\13\
- **HORIZON** (`k`): the rest of Kanto standing on the skyline. The maps were\13\
  never missing -- the game already knows where eight to twenty-one of them\13\
  sit relative to you -- they were just never drawn.\13\
- **ANIME** (OFF / CEL / FULL): cel-banded light, rim light and an ink line,\13\
  with no new render pass at any rung.\13\
- **IMPACT**: hand-drawn sprite-sheet effects (CC0 packs, see\13\
  `assets/vfx/LICENSE.md`).\13\
\13\
Every sky change above was isolated and measured rather than eyeballed -- they\13\
all landed in one shader, where a screenshot cannot tell you which of them\13\
moved. The whole lot costs under 5% of a sky paint, measured at a ceiling the\13\
game never actually reaches.\13\
\13\
## Previously, in 1.18.0-mobile\13\
\13\
The tall grass is geometry out here, and that release made it behave like it.\13\
\13\
- **WIND / AUTO**, the new default. BREEZE and GALE are two fixed windows onto\13\
  the same climate, so keeping a storm feeling like a storm meant a trip back\13\
  to the options menu every time the sky changed. AUTO spans both on one\13\
  curve: near-still on a calm night, breeze by day, gale on its own under a\13\
  front.\13\
- **Grass that bends instead of sliding.** The tip drops as it goes over\13\
  rather than stretching sideways, every tuft has its own stiffness and phase\13\
  so a meadow is many plants rather than one animated surface, and the gust\13\
  arrives in bands that travel across it.\13\
- **Weather lands ON the grass.** Rain is weight: it damps the sway and adds a\13\
  fast tick as drops hit. Settled snow bows the tufts over, stiffens them, and\13\
  now piles white on the crowns with green showing underneath -- before this,\13\
  a meadow stood green beside ground that had gone white.\13\
- **Walk through it and it lies down**, springs back past upright, and leaves\13\
  a **trail** behind you that recovers over a few seconds. Stop, turn round,\13\
  and the way you came is still there.\13\
- **Wind you can see off the grass**: dust on a clear day, spray under a\13\
  shower, blown white under a fall -- plus a gust front that crosses the frame\13\
  as a line while the meadow bows under it.\13\
\13\
## Source\13\
\13\
https://github.com/BrenoBertucci/Terrarium\13\
\13\
Upstream: https://github.com/DramaticShape/DramaticShapeVoxelMod\13\
",
