    ["absol89/DramaticShapeVoxelMod"] = {
      checkedAt = 1786303482,
      latest = "1.7.6",
      releases = {
        [1] = {
          body = "<img width=\"1822\" height=\"635\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2c21c320-921c-4c32-97c0-17a06cc3f393\" />\13\
\13\
Added 2 new options, that will override your sprite gen choices for front-animated/static and back-animated/static.\13\
What this lets you do is to have another sprite modifying mod like [SHINY](https://github.com/TheRhysWyrill/crystal_animated_sprites_with_shiny_visuals/tree/main), and fallback to those sprites and enjoy it.\13\
\13\
I have also merged a PR that fixes the transparency rendering on the SHINY mod's animated crystal sprites. Love it!\13\
\13\
If you enable these 2 options (ON) without having another sprite modifying mod, you get ROM sprites, but can do:\13\
* Animated player intros with ROM pokemon battle sprites from Red and Blue on those specific ROM versions.\13\
* Static player backsprite with ROM pokemon battle sprites from Red and Blue on those specific ROM versions.\13\
* I have now added gen1 pokemon yellow front and back sprites to be selectable in animated and static modes.\13\
\13\
Also merged some other minor and seemingly safe PR's from the upstream DramaticShapeVoxelMod on github.\13\
\13\
### Released since 1.7.2\13\
\13\
Changes the folder path and mod ID to BATTLE_ART_VOXEL_FORK, and merges some fixes for UI consistency in battles.\13\
1. Made option HUD SCALING, with OG and SCALED option, where OG is meant to be used with UI like experience bar.\13\
2. Forced BATTLE BG: WHITE so that there is no black bars in Arena. ARENA FILL: WHITE is different, see previous v1.68.\13\
3. Changed textboxes in battle to have an opaque white backplate with black text, like original games. No transparency\13\
4. Merged an iOS compatibility patch for transparent Player HUD, and Opponent HUD. But not for textbox. See link ([PR](https://github.com/DramaticShape/DramaticShapeVoxelMod/pull/119))\13\
5. Removed unneccessary options like TEXTBOX FILL.\13\
6. I wasn't able to change how the intro battle camera behaved to not jump. Instead, added a new player.png of ASH :)\13\
7. I tested and am waiting on a compatibility patch for Kanto in First Person, because I have changed the ID/path now.\13\
\13\
<img width=\"1397\" height=\"804\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/df0b80cf-0c85-4dc9-b587-5e2260f210aa\" />\13\
\13\
Tested on windows with gen1recomp v0.1.75 Aug 6.\13\
\13\
Edit: Added a Kanto First Person 1.57.2 compatible update to 1.7.6 with a voxel cache and Android rendering water.lua",
          downloads = 552,
          name = "1.7.6 BATTLE ART",
          prerelease = false,
          published = "2026-08-06",
          tag = "1.7.6",
          version = "1.7.6",
          zip = {
            name = "BATTLE_ART_VOXEL_FORK-1.7.6.zip",
            size = 20922176,
            url = "https://github.com/absol89/DramaticShapeVoxelMod/releases/download/1.7.6/BATTLE_ART_VOXEL_FORK-1.7.6.zip",
          },
        },
        [2] = {
          body = "Just adding demo backsprites and scaled trainer portraits, and animated back and front sprites for 151 pokemon. This is a proof of concept private mod release based on the work of the https://github.com/bryanthaboi/gen1recomp project and https://github.com/DramaticShape/DramaticShapeVoxelMod/commit/6e9b787e4124c6d1aeaeead841d5052e34290e01 as they were in 1.5.1 and tweaked on 4 Aug 2026. Have fun!\13\
\13\
1. Reduced and refined tilt-shift blur for a clearer battlefield and overworld.\13\
2. Improved battle camera framing, sprite anchoring, native-resolution scaling, shadows, and world/UI placement.\13\
3. Balanced enemy and player HUD scale, spacing, transparency, contrast, and readability. Trainer art at 2x size.\13\
4. Added static and animated Battle Art modes with front/back generation selectors and reliable ROM fallbacks.\13\
5. Added bring-your-own-sprites support for Pokémon and trainer artwork without per-sprite Lua files.\13\
6. Added animated atlas decoding and player-intro animation support. Version 1.60 also adds an animated redplayer\13\
9. Merged upstream fixes to DramaticShapeVoxelMod, improving water and voxels. Made iOS ui upright but opaque.\13\
10. Changed the manifest to point to the fork repo and upped the tag to 1.60 to avoid confusing update notification.\13\
11. Changed trainer sprite size back to 1x for version 1.63. You can select gen3 trainer art if you want bigger trainers.\13\
12. Selectively picked free camera updates to 1st person and 3rd person camera modes, for the v1.65 updated builds.\13\
\13\
Modified with chatGPT 5.6 sol light.\13\
\13\
<img width=\"1891\" height=\"860\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1a4bbdd4-43a1-43f3-8e29-a4f46ddf378e\" />\13\
\13\
Adjusted blur at the top and bottom of the screen, removed camera zoom in/out of battle, and adjusted sprite anchoring.\13\
\13\
<img width=\"1020\" height=\"763\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1e62bdb7-ff39-4747-bb5b-03094d2ea429\" />\13\
\13\
Scaled trainer sprites and put them in world scale. Also adjusted the UI to keep a consistent color throughout the battles.\13\
\13\
Ask me about the release here on X. Version update to 1.6.5 brings improvements to water rendering and voxel graphics.\13\
Optionally, if you play on iOS, you can try the v1.53 build instead. It will have white backgrounds on UI elements (upright)\13\
\13\
<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet\" data-media-max-width=\"560\"><p lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">So <a href=\"https://x.com/ChatGPT?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw\">@ChatGPT</a> and me put animated gen5 backsprites and scaled <a href=\"https://x.com/hashtag/pokemon?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw\">#pokemon</a> trainer sprites onto a camera zoom PR \13\
<a href=\"https://t.co/Qkv2z5HMZN\">pic.twitter.com/Qkv2z5HMZN</a></p>&mdash; Eric (@absol_89) <a href=\"https://x.com/absol_89/status/2083297398806184125?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw\">July 31, 2026</a></blockquote>\13\
\13\
While this is a mod, it only works with the original gen1recomp project. They have supplied an MIT licence which is below:\13\
Note: The changed sprites are not part of the source code. It is only for personal entertainment if you own Black 2/White 2\13\
\13\
